  "language": "en",
  "text": "2.3 1 Maasin Rum in India is sometimes a very wet place. The rainy season is between May and September each year. At this time of the year, up to 330 cm of rain fall every month. 2 Tromsø is a town in Norway. It's very far north, and in the winter it's very dark. The sun doesn't come up at all for four weeks. 3 During the dry season in parts of Africa, many animals travel a long way to find water. Some elephants travel more than a hundred kilometers. 4 In New England, in the US, autumn begins in September and ends in November. It's a great place to see the red and orange colors on the trees. 5 In Australia, summer is in the months of December, January and February. It's a good time to go to the beach, because the weather at this time is sometimes very hot. It can be more than 50 degrees Celsius. 6 In the Atlas Mountains in Morocco, lots of roses appear in the spring. These flowers look and smell beautiful. In May each year, people take the flowers and use them in perfume and in tea.",
